      "data": {
        "text": "**Developing Error Log Queries**\n\nI've just finished the initial setup, creating the `query_error_logs.py` file. I've imported `os` and `google.cloud.logging`, and I'm now working on the `query_error_logs` function. It will take `project_id` and `severity` to filter logs, and I'm currently figuring out the best way to handle the additional filtering parameters.\n\n\n**Finalizing Implementation Details**\n\nI've completed the error log query functionality. The code now includes the `query_error_logs` function that accepts `project_id`, `severity`, and `time_range`. It leverages Google Cloud Logging, constructs a filter string incorporating severity and a timestamp derived from the `time_range`. I've added a helper function, `time_range_to_timestamp`, and included example usage in the `main` block. I have verified that the project provider is Google Cloud Logging. The implementation is complete.\n\n\n",
